A||||7||72vinman||I can't seem to put her away for the winter.||||9||
Z||000000||72vinman||11-12-2001||01:23 AM||||I had planned on putting my GT away for the winter three weeks ago, but I can't seem to do it. I keep telling myself just one more day and then away she goes but if it does not snow then how can I turn my back on her. Maybe it's late and I'm tired, if I sleep now I will make more sense in the morning.<BR>Any tips I should keep in mind if I eventually find the will to put her away. Someone mentioned to me that I should fill the tank up and add some fuel stabilizer for the long winter. Any thoughts. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin1_1.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||tgowens||11-12-2001||01:50 AM||||Thoughts? Only one.......... come down here where it's warm!!!<P>(Great signature!!)<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||11-12-2001||05:44 PM||||I feel the same way.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Poor fiero has to sit all winter with no fun. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000003||California Kid||11-12-2001||06:04 PM||||Have been taking mine out too and enjoying it. The weather has just been too nice not to! Engine just loves that cool air, must be making an extra 15hp!!!<P>As far as any winter prep goes...if you're going to start it every couple weeks, just put in a small bottle of dry gas. No need to put in a conditioner as long as you topped it off with a good grade premium.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Leadfoot||11-12-2001||06:05 PM||||Amen!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||firstfiero||11-12-2001||07:11 PM||||     We don't get much snow here and I have a crappy paint job so I drive mine all year round. I love this weather. The car is definitly quicker and you can fish tail at the drop of a hat. <P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||72vinman||11-12-2001||07:54 PM||||Thanks for the advise California Kid. I know what you mean about this weather. My car seems to just love it. But I know it won't last so I am enjoying evry day I get.||||reg||14
Z||000007||GarethWright||11-13-2001||01:41 AM||||I can't afford a winter beater, so mine gets fun on ice and snow.  When it snows around here, its either gone by afternoon, or here for the duration.  Last year people were driving around my neighborhood while it was still thin, it all compacted to ice, and froze solid overnight, not much fun when you live a mile from the main roads.  The one upside is that the local road crews use sand instead of chemicals or salt, so I dont have to worry as much about rust.  But, theres nothing like a few tons of sand on the road when the snow melts, its almost as slick.||||reg||1
